import ad as ad
// ROUND 4 WAVE 8 (G190 (c), lead decision): the gradient buffer here shares
// storage with an array the derivative reads (identity(..) beside the
// buffer, or a module alias of it), which is now REFUSED at lowering in every
// lane (BL4005); the program stays as the refusal witness of its shape.
// ============================================================================
// PM40 (rule `ad-checkpoint v1`, opt-in) DECLINES: `forcing` is a closure
// returned by `factory`, capturing the gradient buffer `backing`; a copy of
// a closure keeps its captured storage, so only a call returning a plain
// dense array is a snapshot target (Codex design review of the wave-6
